Here is an example of how this could be achieved:
```
const micromark = require('micromark');

const labelParser = {
  parse: (text) => {
   const markup = micromark(text);
   const labels = [];
   markup.forEach((node) => {
     if (node.type === 'label') {
       labels.push(node.value);
     }
   });
   return labels;
  },
};

const labels = labelParser.parse("This is a test label!");
console.log(labels); // Output: ["test"]
```
This code uses the `micromark` library to parse the input text and extract any labels found in the text. The `labelParser` object defines a `parse` method that takes a string of text as input, parses it using `micromark`, and then iterates over the parsed nodes to find any labels. The `labels` array is returned at the end of the `parse` method.

