response_prompt:
**app/components/base-component.js**

```js
import Component from '@ember/component';
import { action } from '@ember/object';

export default class BaseComponent extends Component {
  // Called when the component is inserted into the DOM
  didInsertElement() {
    this._clickHandler = this._handleClick.bind(this);
    this.element.addEventListener('click', this._clickHandler);
  }

  // Called just before the component is removed from the DOM
  willDestroyElement() {
    this.element.removeEventListener('click', this._clickHandler);
    this._clickHandler = null;
  }

  // Generic click handler that looks for the `trackClick` attribute
  _handleClick(event) {
    // Find the closest ancestor (or self) that has the attribute
    const target = event.target.closest('[trackClick]');
    if (!target) { return; }

    // Grab the value of the attribute
    const value = target.getAttribute('trackClick');

    // If the component defines an `elementClicked` method, call it
    if (typeof this.elementClicked === 'function') {
      this.elementClicked(value);
    }
  }
}
```

**app/components/my-component.js**

```js
import BaseComponent from './base-component';
import { action } from '@ember/object';

export default class MyComponent extends BaseComponent {
  @action
  elementClicked(someValue) {
    // Your custom logic here
    console.log('Clicked element with trackClick value:', someValue);
  }
}
```

**app/templates/components/my-component.hbs**

```hbs
<div>
  <button trackClick="button1">Button 1</button>
  <a href="#" trackClick="link1">Link 1</a>
  <span trackClick="span1">Some text</span>
</div>
```

**How it works**

1. `BaseComponent` attaches a single click listener to the component’s root element when it is inserted into the DOM.
2. The listener checks whether the click originated from an element (or its descendant) that has the `trackClick` attribute.
3. If such an element is found, the listener reads the attribute’s value and, if the component defines an `elementClicked` method, calls it with that value.
4. Every component that needs this behaviour simply extends `BaseComponent` instead of `Component`. No per‑component template changes are required beyond adding the `trackClick` attribute to the desired elements.

